nt (\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}})\\,\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245294} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e33c61-ce7d-5d6f-8b48-2ec3df936b59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int (\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}-2\\sqrt{u})\\,\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246213} {:answer/id #uuid "d9a63738-1fc7-516b-8a74-f5df9e4c8108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}-2\\sqrt{u})\\,\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "563ddb72-a5d5-5545-b652-e213a8e8b275" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int (\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}-2\\sqrt{u}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}})\\,\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245073} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9ed1f13-56b9-5ca5-8bae-6de6c8b90d03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246936}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e1a79b4-288f-5893-a2f8-463fb8d4ce10" :question/math-academy-id "q-113751" :question/problem "Given that $u=x+1,$ which integral is equivalent to $\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u=x+1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe also note that \n$x=u-1.$\n\nNow we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{(u-1)^{2}}{\\sqrt{u}}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int ({u}^{2}-2u+1){u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int ({u}^{3/2}-2{u}^{1/2}+{u}^{-1/2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int (\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}-2\\sqrt{u}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}})\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259761 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1207805e-dbad-515d-bc59-d46dd549c7b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{45}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{27}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256947} {:answer/id #uuid "23b06bd9-e43a-5ce9-a4e7-de33b7c00919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257082} {:answer/id #uuid "3608d43b-fbe5-5b9b-bd38-918370a2164f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{45}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{3}}+С" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257257} {:answer/id #uuid "7942ecf7-c33c-59a7-b547-e0aad2228d8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{3}}+С" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257854} {:answer/id #uuid "b1c1b674-3f07-5054-8b62-29b4dede0eb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{27}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1207805e-dbad-515d-bc59-d46dd549c7b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{45}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{27}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256947} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f415475-9d2f-5036-8871-5dd5bdc3295b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259083}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf091dac-5b0f-53e6-bd72-c4b61f020711" :question/math-academy-id "q-12497" :question/problem "$\\int x\\sqrt{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3x+1.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n$x=\\frac{u-1}{3}.$\n\nNow we can solve the integral in terms of $u,$ and then express our final answer in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\sqrt{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{u-1}{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int ({u}^{3/2}-{u}^{1/2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(\\frac{1}{5/2}{u}^{5/2}-\\frac{1}{3/2}{u}^{3/2})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}-\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{45}{u}^{5/2}-\\frac{2}{27}{u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{45}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{27}\\sqrt{(3x+1)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292607 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0823988f-305f-5042-86ff-7315214a31b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{(z+4)^{3}}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{z+4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290675} {:answer/id #uuid "a9614fed-ed70-5eeb-8b61-ef77a1571c6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{(z+4)^{2}}}{3}+2\\sqrt{z+4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291371} {:answer/id #uuid "e171b6e4-226a-545c-8c9d-45a8021fc3ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{(z+4)^{3}}}{3}+2\\sqrt{z+4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291576} {:answer/id #uuid "e8550de6-d465-50e3-8f25-691b00066a39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt[3]{(z+4)^{2}}}{3}+\\sqrt{z+4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291604} {:answer/id #uuid "ea441298-6bab-5b87-8ecb-0704d0aba5b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt[3]{(z+4)^{2}}}{3}+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{z+4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e171b6e4-226a-545c-8c9d-45a8021fc3ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{(z+4)^{3}}}{3}+2\\sqrt{z+4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291576} :answer-field/id #uuid "0207284d-a167-59ba-b0a2-915166f15039" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291738}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7de83625-3bca-5002-8a64-075a352f81b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-2592" :question/problem "Find the integral of $\\frac{z+5}{\\sqrt{z+4}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=z+4.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}z}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}z=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n$z+5=u+1.$\n\nNow we can solve the integral in terms of $u,$ and then express our final answer in terms of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{z+5}{\\sqrt{z+4}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\frac{u+1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{u}{\\sqrt{u}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\int \\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u+\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u+\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2{u}^{3/2}}{3}+2\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{(z+4)^{3}}}{3}+2\\sqrt{z+4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292610 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3244d82b-0c46-53a8-a660-f9290373702b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{7}}-\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt[5]{(1-x)^{4}}+\\sqrt{(1-x)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290834} {:answer/id #uuid "39d5bebf-6cd0-585d-82cb-e1a9d8d22ac7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}\\sqrt[5]{(1-x)^{7}}+\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt[5]{(1-x)^{4}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt[5]{(1-x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290873} {:answer/id #uuid "832e2443-c62a-52bc-a01a-c04f3bfe80ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{7}}+\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291188} {:answer/id #uuid "9dbb02ca-90cb-5702-8097-54a2c304eaff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{7}-{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291317} {:answer/id #uuid "ef92ec5b-c1fe-5e63-956a-e6526b88cd0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{{x}^{9}}+\\frac{2}{7}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{5}{3}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "832e2443-c62a-52bc-a01a-c04f3bfe80ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{7}}+\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291188} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0bc0d7e-9c01-5db9-a9e1-8f9aad1e4e7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292282}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "056e1c78-a9bb-5b9a-a3a2-7b12402a4162" :question/math-academy-id "q-2615" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int {x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=1-x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n$x=1-u.$\n\nNow we can solve the integral in terms of $u,$ and then express our final answer in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int (1-u)^{2}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\int ({u}^{2}-2u+1)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\int ({u}^{5/2}-2{u}^{3/2}+{u}^{1/2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-(\\frac{2}{7}{u}^{7/2}-\\frac{4}{5}{u}^{5/2}+\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{7}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{7}}+\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292611 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d6d8f53-a600-58bb-9317-00c4a396aa39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\sqrt{(4-x)^{3}}+\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(4-x)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290754} {:answer/id #uuid "25d24972-54bd-5282-81f4-d205290af08a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{(4-x)^{3}}+\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{(4-x)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290790} {:answer/id #uuid "333c2baf-7288-5195-91b2-e899a0052507" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt[3]{4-x}-\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(4-x)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290837} {:answer/id #uuid "45750a92-c47c-5aea-bf8b-0739cb26aa37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\sqrt{(2x+1)^{3}}+\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(2x+1)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290918} {:answer/id #uuid "6e50a711-1c63-5b6e-8f33-5faec0a6f08b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{(2x+1)^{3}}-\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{(2x+1)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d6d8f53-a600-58bb-9317-00c4a396aa39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\sqrt{(4-x)^{3}}+\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(4-x)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290754} :answer-field/id #uuid "78a48d79-4b02-5ea6-ba8f-a1a025670875" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292115}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a9848d15-ae9b-5ed7-b76d-7cc1c522f111" :question/math-academy-id "q-2621" :question/problem "Calculate the integral of $(2x+1)\\sqrt{4-x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=4-x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n$x=4-u.$\n\nNow we can solve the integral in terms of $u,$ and then express our final answer in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2x+1)\\sqrt{4-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2(4-u)+1)\\sqrt{u}(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\int (9-2u)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\int (9{u}^{1/2}-2{u}^{3/2})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-(6{u}^{3/2}-\\frac{4}{5}{u}^{5/2})+C \\\\  & =-6\\sqrt{(4-x)^{3}}+\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(4-x)^{5}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323705 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c8afaaf-a5a3-5817-9902-4b9f1aac1f4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{3}}+\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321247} {:answer/id #uuid "9f95c7f4-5e6b-586f-ae10-c289a531d382" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{3}}+\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{x-2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322406} {:answer/id #uuid "9fbb104b-0fb9-5582-bfd6-dc3f62edffec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}+\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322410} {:answer/id #uuid "c3d1bb0f-ad9a-5731-9e49-51434344674d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322667} {:answer/id #uuid "e4779ab1-85e6-5cde-9a88-7152ff7f24f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{5}}+\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4779ab1-85e6-5cde-9a88-7152ff7f24f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{5}}+\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322937} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c125c50-7106-5844-8cef-6ffbad450d24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323472}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5fcbe8de-e8a0-5eba-b6a1-83fd9a0bf22e" :question/math-academy-id "q-3566" :question/problem "Find the integral of $x\\sqrt{x-2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=x-2.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n$x=u+2.$\n\nNow we can solve the integral in terms of $u,$ and then express our final answer in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\sqrt{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (u+2)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{3/2}+2{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}+\\frac{4}{3}{u}^{3/2})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{5}}+\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323708 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a611287-2092-535b-876a-6227f0cdbe6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{5}}+\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321593} {:answer/id #uuid "40303fb5-ad09-5651-9e6d-477357934177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321653} {:answer/id #uuid "da406410-10fc-5b41-98bc-806eaf0b8b07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{5}}+\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322857} {:answer/id #uuid "ec742af6-9a42-5865-b47a-026a427907d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{3}}+\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323006} {:answer/id #uuid "ec7b991e-7735-537a-9dcf-9e46202592a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}+\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da406410-10fc-5b41-98bc-806eaf0b8b07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{5}}+\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322857} :answer-field/id #uuid "591d5ee9-0682-5b74-a347-5bacb1425e6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323341}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3890b150-4353-5f13-8433-5ec211c68375" :question/math-academy-id "q-3568" :question/problem "$\\int {x}^{3}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={x}^{2}-1.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n${x}^{2}=u+1.$\n\nNow we can solve the integral in terms of $u,$ and then express our final answer in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{3}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (u+1)\\cdot \\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (u+1){u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{3/2}+{u}^{1/2})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}+\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{5}}+\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-1)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332707 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d518d37-c7ae-5a1f-a0d7-975836876bc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int ({u}^{6/5}-{u}^{1/5})\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330068} {:answer/id #uuid "22416b44-6976-5c1a-98e0-b980f491c8e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {u}^{6/5}\\,\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330243} {:answer/id #uuid "2c9f6d49-cb40-5e76-b341-e228fcbb45f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {u}^{1/5}\\,\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330346} {:answer/id #uuid "c9966b80-b9d5-57ac-825e-ea0bad9d0755" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int ({u}^{6/5}+{u}^{1/5})\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331733} {:answer/id #uuid "e11b0cfa-c722-5383-90f9-ba1ea47846a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int ({u}^{1/5}+{u}^{-1/5})\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9966b80-b9d5-57ac-825e-ea0bad9d0755" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int ({u}^{6/5}+{u}^{1/5})\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331733} :answer-field/id #uuid "eed8005f-5fb3-571e-8c62-3dc3d9cb1264" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332621}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d725487a-5806-5f7e-95bc-a9839bf05cf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-49386" :question/problem "Given that $u=x-1$, which integral is equivalent to $\\int x\\sqrt[5]{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u=x-1,$ then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n$x=u+1.$\n\nNow we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\sqrt[5]{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (u+1)(\\sqrt[5]{u})(\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int (u+1)({u}^{1/5})(\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int ({u}^{6/5}+{u}^{1/5})\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332708 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "027ccbbd-79ba-5d67-8599-c6645b801c11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{1/2}+{u}^{-1/2})\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329987} {:answer/id #uuid "844f0a0b-95d9-53ea-83cb-1576d7223aaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{1/2}-{u}^{-1/2})\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331125} {:answer/id #uuid "91b35456-97f5-5ca0-a329-1699c5d10e19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\int ({u}^{1/2}-{u}^{-1/2})\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331248} {:answer/id #uuid "db77fa6b-b561-58ac-b36c-844e170a1f92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331893} {:answer/id #uuid "e8ac5c0c-f8e1-538e-a058-d5226be5735b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "844f0a0b-95d9-53ea-83cb-1576d7223aaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{1/2}-{u}^{-1/2})\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331125} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc4d9a6a-230e-54a2-a466-e038c2c827ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332529}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e0542bde-b2c9-57c4-9ab2-47066e6c42b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-49387" :question/problem "Given that $u=1+{x}^{2}$, which integral is equivalent to $\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u=1+{x}^{2}$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,x\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n${x}^{2}=u-1$\n\nNow we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}} & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\cdot x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (u-1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{1/2}-{u}^{-1/2})\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332732 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c6ac662-8602-509a-8dfc-93dcf566258d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\int ({u}^{1/3}-u)\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330058} {:answer/id #uuid "8f6c7746-9678-57df-be33-8ed06413d2db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{4/3}+{u}^{1/3})\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331219} {:answer/id #uuid "af647b68-b83c-5c45-a5e7-b73eca810d4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{5/3}-{u}^{2/3})\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331497} {:answer/id #uuid "afc3faa8-9c98-5356-9135-be03c3fc2f99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\int ({u}^{4/3}-{u}^{1/3})\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331505} {:answer/id #uuid "e4343c4a-5211-5da4-b722-c14ebb98fb22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{4/3}+{u}^{1/3})\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afc3faa8-9c98-5356-9135-be03c3fc2f99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\int ({u}^{4/3}-{u}^{1/3})\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331505} :answer-field/id #uuid "34e105ad-f638-5136-8028-88116f06b516" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332291}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83445e9a-9a7b-5343-94bb-fbcbc7a0d63e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49528" :question/problem "Given that $u=2x+1$, which integral is equivalent to $\\int x\\sqrt[3]{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u=2x+1$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also note that $x=\\frac{1}{2}(u-1).$\n\nNow we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\sqrt[3]{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(u-1)(\\sqrt[3]{u})(\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int (u-1)({u}^{1/3})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int ({u}^{4/3}-{u}^{1/3})\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Indefinite Integrals of Algebraic Functions Using Substitution"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166784 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166622 :question/id #uuid "ff40db23-6bc1-539b-9f67-3c72c6f448d5" :question/math-academy-id "e-8405" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral\n$\\displaystyle \\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits} \\displaystyle \\int_{-2}^{1} \\sinh {\\left(2x+1\\right)} \\, \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nu=2x+1\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x} = 2 \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x=\\dfrac 1 2 \\, \\textrm d u\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u$.\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x & -2 & 1 \\\\ u & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{-2}^{1}\\sinh (2x + 1)dx &= \\int_{-3}^{3}\\sinh u \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\int_{-3}^{3}\\sinh udu \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{1}{2}\\cosh u\\right|_{-3}^{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(\\cosh 3 - \\cosh (-3)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(\\cosh 3 - \\cosh 3) \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6f89636-f9bd-563d-a489-2a16746f8707" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048332 :topic/math-academy-id 1159 :topic/title "Calculating Definite Integrals Using Substitution"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049599 :topic/math-academy-id 304 :topic/title "Integrating Hyperbolic Functions"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0c6d3e3-d886-5411-857f-753198ba6a07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\cosh (4x + 3) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165489} {:answer/id #uuid "c52538ac-015d-53d5-985e-50d6b764441e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\cosh (4x - 3) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165490} {:answer/id #uuid "01f3e4f0-fe38-5df6-a524-ae09c8e207f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\cosh (4x - 3) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165491} {:answer/id #uuid "22bdcbb6-c2ee-5663-9bf2-f0840b71d726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\cosh (4x - 3) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165492} {:answer/id #uuid "6f608518-f100-5576-a620-e54497be030f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cosh (4x - 3) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165493}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a271c815-