db/ref 17592186482685} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b44bec1a-ceeb-51a2-9ac7-7f7c3daabea8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x -y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b44bec1a-ceeb-51a2-9ac7-7f7c3daabea8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x -y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482691} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1c9ea17-9868-5c6c-b839-1ebe7eceb2e8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482701}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e25fd592-804a-557b-ae2e-2341670e35ba" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(-2,3)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(3,-1)$ and $(6, 5)$. Write your answer in **standard form.** Use $Ax+By=C$ with integer $A,B,C$, $A>0$, and coprime $A$ and $B$ (their greatest common divisor is $1$). Enter $Ax+By$ in the first blank and $C$ in the second blank.\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(3,-1)$ and $(6,5)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m &= \\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1} \\\\ &= \\frac{5-(-1)}{6-(3)} \\\\ &= 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of $2$ and passes through the point $(-2,3)$. To find the equation of this line, we use point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 &= m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(3) &= 2(x-(-2)) \\\\ y-(3) &= 2 x + 4 \\\\ y &= 2 x + 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, write the equation in standard form with coprime integer coefficients and a positive $x$-coefficient.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2 x + 7 \\\\ 2 x -y &= -7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first blank is $2 x -y$ and the second blank is $-7$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Working With Lines in Standard Form"}]}
